{"name":"Neckmaxxing / neck training","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":36,"casual":{"lead":["Neckmaxxing is training the neck muscles to make the neck thicker, which proponents say gives a more masculine, dominant look and better balance between the head, jaw and body. It is described on looksmax.org as a softmaxx.","Neck exercises load the muscles around the cervical spine, with the sternocleidomastoid named in forum guides as the muscle that thickens the neck from the front. Forum posts offer ratio targets, such as neck width to bigonial (jaw) width near 1:1 or a neck-to-height ratio near 1.35, and say a wider neck makes a narrow head and jaw look more in proportion. These are community conventions; no published study validates them and no clinical studies of neck training for appearance were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People follow forum guides using neck curls, extensions and similar loaded movements added to a lifting routine, and track neck width with a tape. A thicker neck builds over months of consistent training."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Loaded neck exercises sit near the cervical spine, and one forum guide calls neck work one of the most dangerous softmaxxes. Gradual loading and careful form are the usual precautions in guides."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"A Systematic Review of Peer-Reviewed Studies on Preventing Sport-Related Concussion (SRC) in Adult Football (Soccer): Mapping Sparce Evidence of Rule Changes and Head-Neck Training.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42121642/","source":"Healthcare (Basel, Switzerland)","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Combining evidence and practice to optimise neck training aimed at reducing head acceleration events in sport: a systematic review and Delphi-consensus study.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40345809/","source":"British journal of sports medicine","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"What Factors Influence Head Acceleration During a Purposeful Header in Soccer Players? A Systematic Review.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40272776/","source":"Sports medicine (Auckland, N.Z.)","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Concussion Reduction in Division I and II Athletes: Effects of Simple Cervical Spine Exercise Regimen.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39229396/","source":"Cureus","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Skull Base Surgery Training and Practice Patterns among Recent Otolaryngology Fellowship Graduates.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27441153/","source":"Journal of neurological surgery. Part B, Skull base","year":2016,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"The role of neuroplasticity in experimental neck pain: a study of potential mechanisms impeding clinical outcomes of training.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24815594/","source":"Manual therapy","year":2014,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Effect of training on corticomotor excitability in clinical neck pain.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24664588/","source":"European journal of pain (London, England)","year":2014,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Training effects of combined resistance and proprioceptive neck muscle exercising.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23640321/","source":"Journal of back and musculoskeletal rehabilitation","year":2013,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Specific neck training induces sustained corticomotor hyperexcitability as assessed by motor evoked potentials.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23609207/","source":"Spine","year":2013,"cites":null,"kind":"Clinical Trial"},{"title":"Neck-shortening effect on prosaccade reaction time formed through saccadic training accompanied by maintenance of neck flexion.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19711093/","source":"European journal of applied physiology","year":2009,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"An electromyographic comparison of neck conditioning exercises in healthy controls.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18550959/","source":"Journal of strength and conditioning research","year":2008,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Effects of neck muscle training in women with chronic neck pain: one-year follow-up study.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16503693/","source":"Journal of strength and conditioning research","year":2006,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Neck training and +Gz-related neck pain: a preliminary study.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9795549/","source":"Military medicine","year":1998,"cites":null,"kind":null}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Neck Training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1732747/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260109075239/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1732747/"},{"title":"Neck training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1416328/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250513055719/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1416328/"},{"title":"Neck training Guide","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-guide.1130900/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240826050938/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-guide.1130900/"},{"title":"neck training is lifefuel","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-is-lifefuel.1077302/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240714101903/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-is-lifefuel.1077302/"},{"title":"neckmaxxing best way to optimize neck gains short thread","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neckmaxxing-best-way-to-optimize-neck-gains-short-thread.1052358/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240626070905/https://looksm