archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251217010853/https://looksmax.org/threads/the-comprehensive-guide-to-neck-training-and-what-most-people-very-get-wrong.1736218/"},{"title":"how to build and have good neck gains with isometrics at home","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-build-and-have-good-neck-gains-with-isometrics-at-home.1727023/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218232506/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-build-and-have-good-neck-gains-with-isometrics-at-home.1727023/"},{"title":"best neck training excersise","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/best-neck-training-excersise.1701937/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218071454/https://looksmax.org/threads/best-neck-training-excersise.1701937/"},{"title":"high iq neck training no excuse not to be doing this","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/high-iq-neck-training-no-excuse-not-to-be-doing-this.1490148/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250829181140/https://looksmax.org/threads/high-iq-neck-training-no-excuse-not-to-be-doing-this.1490148/"},{"title":"whats the best neck training routine","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-best-neck-training-routine.1468822/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250812113047/https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-best-neck-training-routine.1468822/"},{"title":"how long does it take to see significant results of neck training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-long-does-it-take-to-see-significant-results-of-neck-training.1024252/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240513214259/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-long-does-it-take-to-see-significant-results-of-neck-training.1024252/"},{"title":"can neck training make my neck too thick","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/can-neck-training-make-my-neck-too-thick.610888/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221127064405/https://looksmax.org/threads/can-neck-training-make-my-neck-too-thick.610888/"},{"title":"i developed really uncomfortable sleep apnea cause of neck training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/i-developed-really-uncomfortable-sleep-apnea-cause-of-neck-training.514344/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220610174705/https://looksmax.org/threads/i-developed-really-uncomfortable-sleep-apnea-cause-of-neck-training.514344/"},{"title":"why does neck training lower my hyoid","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/why-does-neck-training-lower-my-hyoid.491025/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220517022020/https://looksmax.org/threads/why-does-neck-training-lower-my-hyoid.491025/"},{"title":"gtfih caution for neck training neckcels","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/gtfih-caution-for-neck-training-neckcels.414881/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211112232737/https://looksmax.org/threads/gtfih-caution-for-neck-training-neckcels.414881/"},{"title":"i got injured by neck training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/i-got-injured-by-neck-training.349761/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250711191028/https://looksmax.org/threads/i-got-injured-by-neck-training.349761/"},{"title":"stupid question do steroids get bigger neck gains","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/stupid-question-do-steroids-get-bigger-neck-gains.341138/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210503045130/https://looksmax.org/threads/stupid-question-do-steroids-get-bigger-neck-gains.341138/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[]},"angle":{"goal":"Jawline & face shape","effect":"indirect","chain":["Thicker neck muscles","Wider neck relative to jaw","More masculine, balanced proportions"],"text":"Neckmaxxers train the neck to make it thicker, which they say adds a masculine, dominant look and better face and frame proportions. A wider neck sits more in balance with the jaw and shoulders. Neck-to-jaw ratio targets circulate on forums, and no published study validates them."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Neckmaxxing is the looksmaxxing practice of training the neck to make it thicker, on the belief that a wider neck contributes to a masculine, dominant look and better facial and frame proportions [1][2].","Forum posts offer ideal ratios, such as a neck-to-bigonial (jaw width) ratio of roughly 0.95 to 1, and in one thread a neck width-to-height ratio near 1.35 [1]. Another guide states the neck should match the width of the widest part of the face and that the bigonial to bizygomatic ratio should be around 0.9 to 1.05 [2]. These are community conventions, and no published study validating them was found.","No clinical studies of neck training for appearance were found."],"infobox":[["Category","Lifestyle / training"],["Target","Neck musculature, including sternocleidomastoid"],["Community ratio target","Neck about equal to bigonial width"],["Clinical studies","None found"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Forum guides describe adding neck exercises, such as neck curls and extensions, to a lifting routine. One author calls the neck among the most dangerous yet rewarding softmaxxes and claims it could add about 0.5 PSL points [2]. PSL is a community rating scale for looks and is not a validated measure."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing","paras":["Posters compare necks to celebrity examples and discuss proportions with the head and jaw, saying that people with a small or narrow skull may already be proportional while those with a wide skull would need to build neck size [1]. A guide on the sternocleidomastoid describes keeping the neck 'packed' during curls [2]. A third thread shows before and after posts."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Research and expert views","paras":["The forum material references a PubMed paper on androgen receptor expression in neck and limb muscles, but its findings are not summarized in the posts [1]. No expert guidance on neck thickness for appearance was found."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Neckmaxxing threads on looksmax.org mix anatomy, ratio targets and training guides [1][2].","claims":[{"claim":"A neck about as wide as the jaw is ideal.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Neck training can add notable rating points to overall looks.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Neck training is risky.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Neckmaxxing","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neckmaxxing.1010943/","source":"looksmax.org","year":null,"type":"forum"},{"title":"nobody understands NECKMAXXING","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/nobody-understands-neckmaxxing.1742596/","source":"looksmax.org","year":null,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Neck Training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1732747/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260109075239/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1732747/"},{"title":"Neck training","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1416328/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250513055719/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training.1416328/"},{"title":"Neck training Guide","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-guide.1130900/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240826050938/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-guide.1130900/"},{"title":"neck training is lifefuel","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-is-lifefuel.1077302/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240714101903/https://looksmax.org/threads/neck-training-is-lifefuel.1077302/"},{"title":"neckmaxxing best way to optimize neck gains short thread","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/neckmaxxing-best-way-to-optimize-neck-gains-short-thread.1052358/","site":"looksmax.org","ar